comments.body:
@participant4 I have changed the scheduled tasks and am now only running Clean Up collections and playlists when i know that the disks are connected. This appears to have fixed the issue.
I have a number of network shares that are mounted shortly after boot where the Jellyfin content is stored. The clean up must have been auto-deleting everything at starup prior to the shares being mounted.
I'm not sure why this only started happening after the Jellyfin updated to 10.9.X, it didnt happen previously. Nonetheless, changeing the cleanup rules for collections and playlists to not run at boot has fixed the issue.
